course: dictionary
lesson: 13088
title: The finale
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A finale is the last part of a show, concert, piece of music or event. It is usually the most exciting part. «The fireworks were the grand finale of the school show.» The clues are grand and the fireworks came at the end, so a finale is the big ending.
explain: Look for clue words like last, end, closing or final. «The whole cast sang together in the finale.» Everyone on stage sang at the end, so the finale is the closing number where the whole show comes together.
explain: On TV, a season finale is the last episode of a season, the one that closes the series for a while. Check your meaning by swapping in end: «The fireworks were the grand end of the school show» still makes sense, so you have found it.
fact: A finale is the last part of a show, concert, piece of music or event.
fact: A finale is usually the most exciting part.
fact: «Grand finale» means a big, impressive ending.
fact: A «season finale» is the last episode of a TV series' season.
fact: The plural of finale is finales.
exercise: «The fireworks were the grand finale of the school show.» What does finale mean? | A list of the cast | The first song of the show | *The last and most exciting part | A short break in the middle
exercise: «The whole cast sang together in the finale.» Who sang in the finale? | *The whole cast | Nobody, it was silent | Only the teacher | Only the youngest children
exercise: «Everyone watched the season finale of their favourite TV show.» What is a season finale? | A film shown on a holiday | The first episode of a new show | A trailer for next year | *The last episode of a TV season
test: «The orchestra played a lively piece as the finale.» What does finale mean here? | *The last part of the concert | A pause for lunch | The tuning before the music | The opening notes
test: Which word means the last part of a show or event? | interval | *finale | prelude | rehearsal
exam: The fourth movement of a symphony is its finale. What does finale mean? | The first part | *The last part | A part for the drums only | The part where the audience leaves
